    "title": "Oklahoma Schools Sound Alarm as Lawmakers Move to Rewrite $88M Tax Rebate - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tara Aguilar ,\n12 hours ago Oklahoma voters will decide Aug. 25 whether to hand state lawmakers new power over how much money flows back to schools and counties under a decades-old manufacturing tax break, a question that has already split the legislature from the school superintendents who depend on that money. State Question 844 would let lawmakers recalculate reimbursement payments owed to local governments for revenue lost to the state's manufacturing property tax exemption. Backers say the current formula lets a handful of wealthy industrial counties soak up an outsized share of the payout, while school leaders warn a change could gut budgets that cover teacher pay, bond debt and new buildings. Read full article\n4",
    "summary": "12 hours ago Oklahoma voters will decide Aug. 25 whether to hand state lawmakers new power over how much money flows back to schools and counties under a decades-old manufacturing tax break, a question that has already split the legislature from the school superintendents who depend on that money. State Question 844 would let lawmakers recalculate reimbursement payments owed to local governments for revenue lost to the state's manufacturing property tax exemption.",
